d_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-11T23:05:06Z","updated_at":"2026-06-14T05:24:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot v4.6.3.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.3.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7260) - AMD Ryzen 9 7900 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 31.14 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf both left and right shift are held down and are then released, only the last key to be released actually gets released. The other key never gets a key release event and continues to be considered held down.\n\nThis is the same issue as https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101384 but only affecting web builds.\n\nIn the MRP I've included multiple input handling routines, using the Input singleton as well as the _input() function and all have this issue.\n\n**This is specific to the shift keys and does not seem to happen with CTRL**\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHold down both shift keys then release them. One is still considered held down on web export. Happens with input actions and raw keycode handling.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[shift-key-issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28858181/shift-key-issue.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/